  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Volkswagen Atlas?",
      "a": "Yes, through a DIMO device. Both listed DIMO device entries report Fuel Percentage, and the DIMO LTE R1 entry also reports Fuel Level in liters. Query the signal with a Vehicle JWT in the Telemetry API, which is a GraphQL API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Volkswagen Atlas with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Volkswagen Atlas?",
      "a": "Idling is listed for both DIMO device entries. Query the Telemetry API segments resource with the idling detection mechanism, which requires a DIMO device and treats periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range as segments. The default idle RPM ceiling is 1000, and you can change it with maxIdleRpm."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect a refuel on a Volkswagen Atlas?",
      "a": "Refuel is listed for both DIMO device entries. Query segments with the refuel detection mechanism, which finds where fuel level rises significantly. The default minimum increase is 15 percent, adjustable with minIncreasePercent."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Volkswagen Atlas mileage?",
      "a": "Odometer is reported by a DIMO device. Call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the resulting verifiable credential through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a vehicle data API for the Volkswagen Atlas, which connects through a DIMO device on 2018 and newer model years. DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. Coverage for this internal combustion engine model is tested rather than expected. DIMO adds vehicle-state depth on top of GPS tracking; it doesn't replace it."
